The original profile estimated Tom as 26 based on his joke “I’m still 26” during a conversation about getting old. Dan has confirmed Tom is the same age as him — 37, three weeks older. This changes the entire framing significantly.

The differences between them — Dan’s verbose over-explanation vs Tom’s punchy minimalism, Dan’s analytical framework vs Tom’s instinctual reactions — are not generational. They are temperamental. These are two men the same age who have lived completely different versions of the same cultural moment and arrived at very different personalities.

